# Vraska's Final Mercy, second mode: "You lose 2 life. Empower Jace 6." Bot1 already controls Jace, the Mind Sculptor, a nontoken
# Jace planeswalker, which empower Jace never touches (the ruling): the first cast creates a blue Jace planeswalker token and
# puts six loyalty counters on it. The second cast, with a Jace token now controlled, cannot make another: it puts six more on the
# same token, which has 12, while Jace, the Mind Sculptor keeps his 3. Bot1 loses 2 life each time (16).

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Mox Sapphire
Jace, the Mind Sculptor
Vraska's Final Mercy
Vraska's Final Mercy
Swamp
Swamp x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Jace, the Mind Sculptor.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Vraska's Final Mercy.Cast
Bot1.Modes(2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Jace Token.Counters.Loyalty = 6
? Bot1.Life = 18
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Vraska's Final Mercy.Cast
Bot1.Modes(2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 16
Bot1.Battlefield.Jace Token.Counters.Loyalty = 12
Bot1.Battlefield.Jace Token.Token = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Jace, the Mind Sculptor.Counters.Loyalty = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 5
